{
    "background_story": "Julius was a talented young artist, known for his captivating paintings that seemed to capture the essence of the human experience. However, his creative genius was often overshadowed by his afflictive struggles with mental health. Julius battled with crippling anxiety and depression, which would often leave him bedridden for days. Despite his best efforts, he found it challenging to find inspiration in the darkness that seemed to surround him. His art became a reflection of his inner turmoil, with bold brushstrokes and vivid colors that conveyed the intensity of his emotions. Julius's afflictive struggles made him more empathetic and understanding of others who suffered in silence. His art became a beacon of hope, inspiring others to confront their own demons and find solace in the creative process.",
